        "Kelada says Mrs. Ramsay's necklace is real and valuable. Mr. Ramsay claims it is an imitation bought cheaply in New York.",
        "They make a bet. Mrs. Ramsay becomes frightened because the necklace is real and probably came from another man while her husband was away.",
        "Kelada examines the pearls, sees they are real, and is about to prove himself right. Then he notices Mrs. Ramsay's desperate expression.",
        "Kelada lies and says the necklace is imitation. He pays Mr. Ramsay one hundred dollars and allows everyone to laugh at him.",
        "The next morning Mrs. Ramsay secretly returns the money to Kelada. The narrator understands Kelada's sacrifice and changes his opinion."
